  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A simple, convenient spot at the Résidence Palazzo Del Mar, on the Promenade de la Mer in Cavalaire, for a sandwich or a quick meal without breaking the bank. French cuisine, a terrace, and a setting confirmed by an active Tripadvisor listing (3.4/5) and a professional Facebook page (lagrignoterie83).</p>
      <p>Useful clarification: this address is on the town-centre seafront/promenade, about a 20-minute walk from the Cavalaire marina — not literally "facing the harbour".</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Expect to pay between €16 and €20 for a meal, an affordable budget that works well for a quick weekday lunch or after the beach. Regarding dogs: the Pages Jaunes and Mappy directories say "animals accepted" and a general tourism site for the region describes the establishment as welcoming to animals, but the establishment itself publishes no rule, and no water point or bowl is mentioned. Call 04 94 64 34 28 before settling in with your dog.</p>
      <p>The 2024-2025 Saveurs guide of the Cavalaire-sur-Mer tourist office (cavalairesurmer.fr) lists La Grignoterie on the Promenade de la Mer, with paninis, salads, steak, chips and sandwiches. Directories describe it as open every day from 11:30am to 6:30pm, with air conditioning and payment by card or meal vouchers.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this is a handy spot for a quick lunch, but call before coming with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Cavalaire seafront and promenade are right nearby, good for a quiet digestive walk before continuing on to the harbour, about twenty minutes away on foot — a good chance to continue on to the <a href="/en/fiche-sentier-littoral">coastal path</a> or the <a href="/en/fiche-bonporteau">Bonporteau beach</a>. If you need it while you're there, the <a href="/en/fiche-veterinaire-tison">Tison veterinary clinic</a> is also in Cavalaire-sur-Mer.</p>
    </div>

